CAT = "sirLiability"; SEG = "LIA"
Q = [
("A server's duty of care toward guests extends to:",
 'Harm on and off premises', ['Only inside the building', 'Only until the bill is paid', 'Only guests under 25'],
 'The course teaches a duty of care both on and off the premises: harm an over-served guest causes on the way home can be foreseeable.'),
('An over-served guest drives off and injures someone. Who may face a civil lawsuit?',
 'Licensee and maybe staff', ['Only the driver', "Only the car's insurer", 'Only the province'],
 'Legal liability is a core course topic: a licensee that over-serves a guest who then causes harm can be sued, alongside the driver, and staff can be named too.'),
('Which step best shows a licensee met its duty of care to an intoxicated guest?',
 'Stop service, arrange a ride', ['Sell them a large coffee', 'Let them sleep in their car', 'Ask them to drive slowly'],
 'Taking reasonable steps, stopping service and helping the guest get home safely, is what a duty of care asks. Coffee or a nap does not sober a driver.'),
("The Criminal Code's 80 mg limit applies to blood alcohol within how long after driving?",
 '2 hours', ['1 hour', '2 hours', '3 hours', '4 hours'],
 'Criminal Code s. 320.14(1)(b) makes it an offence to have 80 mg or more of alcohol in 100 mL of blood within two hours after driving.',
 'fixed'),
("Which choice removes the impaired driving risk for a guest who has been drinking?",
 "Not driving at all", ["Eating before leaving", "Drinking coffee first", "Driving under the limit"],
 "Food and coffee do not lower BAC, and even below the limit alcohol impairs driving. The only choice with no impaired driving risk is not driving."),
('An intoxicated guest heads for their car keys. Staff should first:',
 'Offer a safe ride', ['Wish them a safe trip', 'Walk them to the car', 'Give them coffee to go'],
 'Reducing impaired driving is a course topic. Offering alternatives such as a taxi, ride-share or a sober friend is the first step.'),
('An intoxicated guest drives away despite your efforts. A responsible next step is:',
 'Call police with details', ['Follow the car yourself', 'Do nothing; they left', 'Post about it online'],
 'Once a drunk driver leaves, calling police with the vehicle description and direction can prevent a crash. Chasing the car puts staff at risk.'),
("Under BC's Act, a driver may have liquor in the vehicle only if it is:",
 'Sealed or out of reach', ['In a cup with a lid', 'In the cup holder', "Under the driver's seat"],
 'Section 76 bars driving with liquor in the vehicle except in listed cases, such as unopened sealed containers or liquor not readily accessible to the driver and passengers.'),
("BC's rule on liquor in a motor vehicle also covers:",
 "Off-road vehicles", ["Only cars on highways", "Only commercial trucks", "Only moving vehicles"],
 "Section 76 defines motor vehicle to include off-road vehicles, and applies even when the vehicle is not moving."),
("Under the Act, a person who is intoxicated in a public place:",
 "May be arrested", ["Must be fined on the spot", "Must be driven home", "Breaks no law"],
 "Section 74 says an intoxicated person must not be or remain in a public place, and a peace officer may arrest them without a warrant."),
('A guest leaves the bar with an open beer to drink on the sidewalk. Under s. 73:',
 'Not allowed', ['Fine if it is beer', 'Fine before 11 p.m.', 'Fine within 10 m'],
 'Section 73 bars drinking or carrying open liquor outside a residence, a private place, a service area or another place the Act allows, such as a designated public area.'),
('Who can be charged when liquor is served to a person showing signs of intoxication?',
 'Licensee and employee', ['Only the licensee', 'Only the guest', 'No one; it is civil'],
 'Section 61(2) applies to a licensee, permittee or employee, and s. 57 makes breaking it an offence, so the server can be charged as well as the licensee.'),
('Section 75 bars anyone from giving liquor to an intoxicated person. It applies to:',
 'Everyone, private hosts too', ['Only licensed staff', 'Only retail clerks', 'Only ticketed events'],
 'Unlike s. 61, which covers licensees and their staff, s. 75 says no person may sell, serve or give liquor to an intoxicated person or one showing signs.'),
("The general manager suspends a pub's licence after repeated over-service. The financial harm falls on:",
 'The business', ['The server on duty', 'The guests', 'The province'],
 'Section 51 lets the general manager impose penalties or suspend a licence. A suspension shuts liquor sales, so the whole business pays for repeated breaches.'),
("Why can a guest's injury after leaving be linked back to the bar?",
 'Harm was foreseeable', ['The bar sold the car', 'The bar charged a cover', 'The guest paid by card'],
 'Liability turns on whether harm was foreseeable and reasonable steps were taken. Serving a visibly intoxicated guest makes a later crash or fall foreseeable.'),
('A licensee wants to reduce its legal risk. Which policy helps most?',
 'Train staff, log refusals', ['Ban water at the bar', 'Cash-only bar tabs', 'Serve doubles only'],
 "Trained staff following a written policy, with incidents recorded, show the licensee took reasonable steps. That is the core of the course's liability topic."),
('A sober guest asks staff to help their drunk friend home. A good response is:',
 'Arrange a safe ride', ['Give the friend a last drink', 'Say it is not our job', "Lend them the bar's car"],
 'Duty of care continues as guests leave. Helping arrange a safe ride, such as a taxi with the sober friend, reduces the risk of harm off the premises.'),
('Over-service raises the risk of which harms that the course aims to reduce?',
 'Impaired driving and violence', ['Higher menu prices', 'Longer opening hours', 'Slower staff training'],
 "Responsible Service BC lists reducing over-consumption, impaired driving and the risk of violence among the course's goals."),
('An off-duty server hosts a house party. Serving a visibly drunk guest there is:',
 'Still an offence', ['Fine at a private home', 'Only a licensee issue', 'Fine if no one drives'],
 'Section 75 applies to every person, not just licensees, so giving liquor to someone showing signs of intoxication is an offence at home too.'),
('A guest who was refused says they will walk home along a busy highway. Staff should:',
 'Help find a safer way', ['Let them go; no car', 'Serve food, then let go', 'Give them a flashlight'],
 'An intoxicated pedestrian is at risk too. The duty of care off premises covers helping guests get home safely, not only stopping drivers.'),
('The best defence against a claim that staff over-served a guest is evidence that staff:',
 'Watched for signs, acted', ['Charged full price', 'Served food late', 'Played music softly'],
 'Showing that staff watched for signs of intoxication, refused service and helped the guest leave safely supports that reasonable care was taken.'),
("Which group does a server's duty of care also protect?",
 'Others the guest may harm', ["Only the server's employer", 'Only paying guests', 'Only the regulars'],
 'The duty of care covers foreseeable harm to third parties, such as other drivers, pedestrians or guests, not only the drinker.'),
("A minor who drank at a bar is injured on the way home. The bar's risk rises because:",
 'Serving a minor is illegal', ['The minor paid in cash', 'The minor sat at a booth', 'Minors heal more slowly'],
 'Supplying liquor to a minor is an offence under s. 77, and breaking the law makes it harder for a licensee to show it took reasonable care.'),
('A server is asked by the owner to keep serving a drunk regular. The server should:',
 'Refuse; it binds servers too', ["Obey the owner's order", 'Serve beer only', 'Serve, then quit'],
 'Section 61 applies to employees as well as licensees, so an instruction from the owner does not make serving an intoxicated guest lawful.'),
]
